<section id="about">

## About

West Ranch Machine Learning brings together students curious about **machine learning** and **artificial intelligence**. In this club, you will learn what machine learning is, including core concepts such as **data**, **training**, and **optimization**; different types of models; and real-world applications of these models. A secondary goal is to promote AI education and literacy.

We meet regularly to collaborate, share knowledge, and build skills that matter in college and beyond.

</section>

<section id="what-we-do">

## What we do

- ### Workshops

  Learn Python, neural networks, and modern ML tools through peer-led sessions.

- ### Projects

  Apply machine learning to campus and community problems across different domains.

- ### Competitions

  Train models and compete in Kaggle, hackathons, and regional STEM challenges.

</section>

